Package: reidentify
Type: Package
Title: Measure Re-Identification Risk in Anonymized Data
Version: 3.0.0
Authors@R: person(given = "@gg_hatano", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "adad0405+reidentify@gmail.com")
Description: Estimates how reliably the records of an anonymized data set can
    be linked back to the individuals in the original data. Per-attribute
    scores are provided for categorical, numeric, set-valued and
    spatio-temporal variables, combined across attributes, and turned into an
    assignment by greedy or optimal ('Hungarian') matching; generalized values
    are also checked for consistency with the original ones. Blocking keeps
    large data tractable. Results are reported as a success rate next to a
    random baseline, together with per-record risk, uniqueness and a
    precision-recall curve, so that a measurement which has quietly stopped
    working is less likely to read as a safe one.
